  "worked_solution": "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2,3}=2\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =1(x-3)(x-(2+3\\text{i}))(x-(2-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-3)(x-(2+3\\text{i}))(x-(2-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)(x-(2+3\\text{i}))(x-(2-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-3)({x}^{2}-x(2-3\\text{i})-x(2+3\\text{i})+(2+3\\text{i})(2-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-3)({x}^{2}-4x+13) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+13x-3{x}^{2}+12x-39 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+25x-39 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+25x-39.$",
